(7115628, 1085955, 61396, '<td valign="top">I like the twist (of bike colorization vs. the dude''s appearance and expression, as well as image orientation). My only request is to pump some air before driving away.</td>', 'I like the twist (of bike colorization vs. the dude''s appearance and expression, as well as image orientation). My only request is to pump some air before driving away.', '2013-10-14 15:37:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7115630, 1085748, 61396, '<td valign="top">spotty but clean is certainly good.</td>', 'spotty but clean is certainly good.', '2013-10-14 15:39:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7115631, 1086005, 61396, '<td valign="top">The Caterpillar and Alice looked at each other for some time in silence: at last the Caterpillar took the <i>hookah</i> out of its mouth, and addressed her in a languid, sleepy voice.<br/> <br/>`Who are YOU?'' said the Caterpillar.<br/> <br/>This was not an encouraging opening for a conversation. Alice replied, rather shyly, `I--I hardly know, sir, just at present-- at least I know who I WAS when I got up this morning, but I think I must have been changed several times since then.''<br/> <br/>ETA: ALICE''S ADVENTURES IN WONDERLAND, by Lewis Carroll, Chapter 5.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-10-16 01:49:08.</i></td>', 'The Caterpillar and Alice looked at each other for some time in silence: at last the Caterpillar took the hookah out of its mouth, and addressed her in a languid, sleepy voice. `Who are YOU?'' said the Caterpillar. This was not an encouraging opening for a conversation. Alice replied, rather shyly, `I--I hardly know, sir, just at present-- at least I know who I WAS when I got up this morning, but I think I must have been changed several times since then.'' ETA: ALICE''S ADVENTURES IN WONDERLAND, by Lewis Carroll, Chapter 5.', '2013-10-14 15:49:14.000000', '2013-10-16 02:49:08.000000', 1),
(7115632, 1086010, 61396, '<td valign="top">good sense of depth</td>', 'good sense of depth', '2013-10-14 15:49:52.000000', NULL, 1),
